Z||000000||Banzai||09-18-2001||01:01 AM||||My dash, as many I've seen, has cracked corners around the lower part of the vents. Not too bad, but bad enough. Is there any way to fix this or have it fixed? Is replacement the ONLY option ????  Thanks<P>Banzai !!!!!!||||reg||5
Z||000001||Nashco||09-18-2001||04:42 AM||||These should be useful:<P> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/009104.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/009104.html</A> <BR> <A HREF="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011414.html" TARGET=_blank>http://www.fiero.nl/forum/Forum2/HTML/011414.html</A> <P>Let us know what you decide on.  FYI, the epoxy I used can be bought at any Autozone for about eight bucks I think.  It is a white box with a green label that says "Epoxy Repair Kit" or something like that.<P>Bryce<BR>88 GT||||reg||1
Z||000002||Monkeyman||09-18-2001||06:20 PM||||Anyone have any suggestions as to what could be used on the corners to keep them from cracking?  Mine are still in perfect condition and I'd like to keep them that way.<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/PontiacAPE.jpg">    <BR>Monkeyman||||reg||1
Z||000003||rockcrawl||09-18-2001||07:54 PM||||Monkeyman,<BR> Someone had suggested razor-sharp metal spikes. That would keep people from banging their knees on them.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Bill Osmer||09-19-2001||01:24 PM||||MM -<P>I would make sure NOT use ArmorAll, but to make sure to use any vinyl cleaner (I use the tirewall shiner). The idea is to not let the vinyl get brittle and crack.<P><P>------------------<BR>Bill Osmer<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/forumcardsig2.jpg"> ||||reg||14
